H4       WHAT THE MECHANISM EXPLAINS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
         EXPLAINS: the 2-TORSION.  Conjugation gives CS = -CS for any manifold with
           an orientation-reversing self-isometry, hence CS in {0, 1/4}.  Derived in
           H2, and an orientation DOUBLE COVER always has such an isometry -- its
           deck transformation -- so its CS is 2-torsion BY CONSTRUCTION.  That is
           B1234's cell 1 (40 of 40 amphichiral) with a reason under it.
         DOES NOT EXPLAIN: the SELECTION OF 0 OVER 1/4.  Conjugation is blind to
           which of the two 2-torsion classes you land in.  L194's hypothesis is
           that FREENESS of the deck involution does the selecting -- and NOTHING IN
           THIS ARC DERIVES THAT.  H3 is data, at a larger slice; it is not a proof,
           and this arc does not let the data imply the theorem.
         SO THE HONEST STATE: B1224 is upgraded from OBSERVED to DERIVED; L194 is
           SHARPENED -- the 2-torsion half is now explained, and exactly the
           selection half remains open, with the evidence for it strengthened.

